# Return the percentage change from old_value to new_value, rounded to one decimal place. If old_value is zero, return 0.0. Otherwise compute (new_value - old_value) / old_value * 100 and round the result to one decimal place using standard rounding. Example: old=150, new=100 -> -33.3; old=0, new=10 -> 0.
